WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
Spin a bicycle wheel on its axle.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.150
Put one dot near the hub,
and another on the rim.

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.800
In one full turn, both dots sweep
through exactly the same angle:

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.460
2 pi radians, or 360 degrees.

5
00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:19.500
Yet the rim dot is a blur, while the
dot near the hub barely seems to move.

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.740
Same wheel, same angle, same time.

7
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.430
So why does the rim move fastest?

8
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.220
In this mission, you'll
measure angles in radians,

9
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.220
and describe a turn with
angular displacement.

10
00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.690
Then you'll reuse the constant-acceleration
equations from straight-line motion,

11
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.330
now for turning.

12
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.740
Your mission: explain why
the rim moves fastest,

13
00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:43.390
when every point turns
through the same angle.
